{"module":"many-targets","voice":"male","duration":263.4,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Many targets: Latino, Asian, Native and immigrant communities","start":0.0,"end":5.55,"words":[[0.05,0.39],[0.39,0.99],[1.29,1.97],[2.27,2.78],[3.08,3.59],[3.59,3.84],[3.84,4.53],[4.53,5.38]]},{"el":"intro","text":"The same machinery of law, mobs and false accusations has been turned on many communities.","start":6.35,"end":12.87,"words":[[6.4,6.56],[6.56,6.89],[6.89,7.55],[7.55,7.71],[7.71,7.96],[8.25,8.57],[8.57,8.82],[8.82,9.15],[9.15,10.05],[10.05,10.3],[10.3,10.54],[10.54,10.87],[10.87,11.03],[11.03,11.36],[11.36,12.27]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Seeing the whole picture builds coalitions, and coalitions pass laws.","start":13.22,"end":18.03,"words":[[13.24,13.63],[13.63,13.78],[13.78,14.08],[14.08,14.54],[14.54,14.92],[14.92,15.76],[16.03,16.26],[16.26,17.02],[17.02,17.25],[17.25,17.55]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Mexican Americans","start":18.38,"end":20.13,"words":[[18.43,19.14],[19.14,19.94]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Historians William Carrigan and Clive Webb documented at least 547 Mexicans lynched in the United States from 1848 to 1928.","start":20.83,"end":30.55,"words":[[20.88,21.53],[21.53,21.91],[21.91,22.36],[22.36,22.56],[22.56,22.88],[22.88,23.07],[23.07,23.78],[23.78,23.91],[23.91,24.17],[24.17,25.58],[25.58,26.16],[26.16,26.55],[26.55,26.68],[26.68,26.81],[26.81,27.32],[27.32,27.71],[27.71,27.97],[27.97,28.8],[28.8,28.93],[28.93,30.09]]},{"el":"s0","text":"In January 1918, Texas Rangers, soldiers and local ranchers killed 15 Mexican men and boys at Porvenir, Texas.","start":30.9,"end":39.92,"words":[[30.95,31.09],[31.09,31.73],[31.73,32.65],[32.9,33.32],[33.32,33.96],[34.21,34.78],[34.78,34.99],[34.99,35.42],[35.42,35.91],[35.91,36.19],[36.19,36.62],[36.62,37.19],[37.19,37.4],[37.4,37.61],[37.61,37.89],[37.89,38.04],[38.04,38.6],[38.85,39.35]]},{"el":"s0","text":"In Mendez v. Westminster (1947), Mexican American families won a case against school segregation in California, seven years before Brown v. Board.","start":40.27,"end":51.77,"words":[[40.31,40.46],[40.46,40.92],[40.92,41.14],[41.52,42.27],[42.27,43.56],[43.82,44.42],[44.42,45.03],[45.03,45.55],[45.55,45.78],[45.78,45.93],[45.93,46.23],[46.23,46.69],[46.69,46.99],[46.99,47.82],[47.82,47.97],[47.97,48.72],[48.99,49.36],[49.36,49.67],[49.67,49.97],[49.97,50.34],[50.34,50.57],[50.95,51.25]]},{"el":"s0","text":"In 1943, servicemen attacked young Mexican Americans in Los Angeles in the “Zoot Suit Riots,” and police arrested the victims.","start":52.12,"end":61.22,"words":[[52.17,52.32],[52.32,53.49],[53.77,54.39],[54.39,54.78],[54.78,55.02],[55.02,55.64],[55.64,56.35],[56.35,56.5],[56.5,56.74],[56.74,57.36],[57.36,57.52],[57.52,57.68],[57.68,57.91],[57.91,58.14],[58.14,58.69],[58.69,58.93],[58.93,59.32],[59.32,59.86],[59.86,60.02],[60.02,60.65]]},{"el":"s0","text":"In 2019 a gunman who had posted about a “Hispanic invasion” killed 23 people at an El Paso Walmart.","start":61.57,"end":69.02,"words":[[61.61,61.75],[61.75,62.7],[62.7,62.85],[62.85,63.29],[63.29,63.43],[63.43,63.65],[63.65,64.16],[64.16,64.53],[64.53,64.67],[64.67,65.26],[65.26,65.84],[65.84,66.13],[66.13,66.79],[66.79,67.15],[67.15,67.3],[67.3,67.45],[67.45,67.59],[67.59,67.96],[67.96,68.47]]},{"el":"s0","text":"(See also the module on borders.)","start":69.37,"end":72.01,"words":[[69.41,69.6],[69.6,70.05],[70.05,70.24],[70.24,70.78],[70.78,70.97],[70.97,71.52]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Asian Americans","start":72.91,"end":74.35,"words":[[72.96,73.38],[73.38,74.14]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Chinese immigrants were massacred in Los Angeles (1871) and Rock Springs (1885) and expelled from Tacoma (1885).","start":75.05,"end":83.73,"words":[[75.1,75.57],[75.57,76.18],[76.18,76.31],[76.31,76.79],[76.79,76.92],[76.92,77.13],[77.13,77.67],[77.67,78.68],[78.92,79.12],[79.12,79.32],[79.32,79.73],[79.73,80.61],[80.84,81.05],[81.05,81.52],[81.52,81.79],[81.79,82.26],[82.26,83.21]]},{"el":"s1","text":"The Chinese Exclusion Act (1882) was the first U.S. law to bar a group by nationality.","start":84.08,"end":90.2,"words":[[84.12,84.26],[84.26,84.74],[84.74,85.36],[85.36,85.56],[85.56,86.32],[86.56,86.77],[86.77,86.91],[86.91,87.18],[87.18,87.52],[87.87,88.0],[88.0,88.14],[88.14,88.28],[88.28,88.42],[88.42,88.69],[88.69,88.9],[88.9,89.65]]},{"el":"s1","text":"About 120,000 Japanese Americans, most of them citizens, were incarcerated during World War II.","start":90.55,"end":98.26,"words":[[90.58,90.91],[90.91,92.55],[92.55,93.07],[93.07,93.73],[93.96,94.29],[94.29,94.42],[94.42,94.61],[94.61,95.2],[95.43,95.56],[95.56,96.35],[96.35,96.81],[96.81,97.07],[97.07,97.2],[97.2,97.79]]},{"el":"s1","text":"In 1982, Vincent Chin was beaten to death in Detroit by two white autoworkers who blamed Japan for lost jobs; they were sentenced to probation and a $3,000 fine, which sparked a national Asian American civil rights movement.","start":98.61,"end":114.6,"words":[[98.65,98.8],[98.8,99.88],[100.15,100.68],[100.68,100.99],[100.99,101.22],[101.22,101.61],[101.61,101.76],[101.76,101.99],[101.99,102.14],[102.14,102.68],[102.68,102.91],[102.91,103.07],[103.07,103.37],[103.37,104.06],[104.06,104.22],[104.22,104.68],[104.68,105.14],[105.14,105.29],[105.29,105.6],[105.6,106.06],[106.33,106.56],[106.56,106.72],[106.72,107.33],[107.33,107.48],[107.48,108.25],[108.25,108.48],[108.48,108.64],[108.64,109.71],[109.71,110.1],[110.36,110.67],[110.67,111.06],[111.06,111.21],[111.21,111.75],[111.75,112.13],[112.13,112.75],[112.75,113.13],[113.13,113.51],[113.51,114.13]]},{"el":"s1","text":"After 9/11, Sikh and South Asian Americans were attacked, starting with the murder of Balbir Singh Sodhi in Arizona days later.","start":114.95,"end":124.14,"words":[[115.0,115.31],[115.31,116.48],[116.75,116.99],[116.99,117.22],[117.22,117.53],[117.53,117.92],[117.92,118.63],[118.63,118.78],[118.78,119.25],[119.52,119.99],[119.99,120.23],[120.23,120.38],[120.38,120.7],[120.7,120.85],[120.85,121.32],[121.32,121.55],[121.55,122.02],[122.02,122.18],[122.18,122.8],[122.8,123.12],[123.12,123.59]]},{"el":"s1","text":"From 2020 to 2021, Stop AAPI Hate received more than 10,000 reports of anti-Asian hate incidents, and in March 2021 a gunman killed eight people, six of them Asian women, at Atlanta-area spas.","start":124.49,"end":138.4,"words":[[124.51,124.78],[124.78,125.6],[125.6,125.74],[125.74,126.83],[127.07,127.34],[127.34,127.54],[127.54,127.82],[127.82,128.23],[128.23,128.36],[128.36,128.57],[128.57,129.25],[129.25,129.66],[129.66,129.79],[129.79,130.48],[130.48,130.75],[130.75,131.43],[131.67,131.87],[131.87,132.01],[132.01,132.28],[132.28,133.3],[133.3,133.44],[133.44,133.85],[133.85,134.12],[134.12,134.33],[134.33,134.74],[134.97,135.25],[135.25,135.38],[135.38,135.59],[135.59,135.93],[135.93,136.34],[136.58,136.71],[136.71,137.6],[137.6,137.94]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Native Americans","start":139.3,"end":140.88,"words":[[139.35,139.88],[139.88,140.68]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Native people were not all granted U.S. citizenship until 1924, and Arizona and New Mexico barred Native people from voting until 1948.","start":141.58,"end":153.33,"words":[[141.63,142.11],[142.11,142.5],[142.5,142.66],[142.66,142.9],[142.9,143.06],[143.06,143.62],[143.62,144.01],[144.41,145.21],[145.21,145.6],[145.6,146.87],[147.15,147.39],[147.39,148.03],[148.03,148.26],[148.26,148.5],[148.5,149.14],[149.14,149.38],[149.38,149.85],[149.85,150.25],[150.25,150.57],[150.57,151.05],[151.05,151.44],[151.44,152.72]]},{"el":"s2","text":"The federal boarding schools are covered in the module on conquest.","start":153.68,"end":157.95,"words":[[153.73,153.89],[153.89,154.44],[154.44,154.84],[154.84,155.24],[155.24,155.32],[155.32,155.72],[155.72,155.88],[155.88,156.04],[156.04,156.51],[156.51,156.67],[156.67,157.39]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Today, American Indian and Alaska Native women face very high rates of violence.","start":158.3,"end":165.82,"words":[[158.36,158.94],[159.28,160.05],[160.05,160.62],[160.62,160.91],[160.91,161.49],[161.49,162.07],[162.07,162.55],[162.55,162.94],[162.94,163.32],[163.32,163.61],[163.61,164.09],[164.09,164.29],[164.29,165.15]]},{"el":"s2","text":"A 2018 Urban Indian Health Institute report noted that of 5,712 cases of missing Native women and girls reported to the FBI's crime database in 2016, only 116 were logged in the federal missing persons database.","start":166.17,"end":179.48,"words":[[166.22,166.34],[166.34,167.02],[167.02,167.25],[167.25,167.59],[167.59,167.81],[167.81,168.33],[168.33,168.61],[168.61,168.95],[168.95,169.12],[169.12,169.24],[169.24,170.94],[170.94,171.28],[171.28,171.39],[171.39,171.68],[171.68,172.02],[172.02,172.3],[172.3,172.47],[172.47,172.7],[172.7,173.1],[173.1,173.21],[173.21,173.33],[173.33,173.72],[173.72,174.01],[174.01,174.52],[174.52,174.63],[174.63,175.43],[175.63,175.91],[175.91,176.99],[176.99,177.1],[177.1,177.33],[177.33,177.45],[177.45,177.56],[177.56,177.96],[177.96,178.24],[178.24,178.58],[178.58,179.15]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Congress passed Savanna's Act and the Not Invisible Act in 2020 to improve how these cases are tracked and investigated.","start":179.83,"end":188.13,"words":[[179.87,180.42],[180.42,180.74],[180.74,181.29],[181.29,181.53],[181.53,181.76],[181.76,181.92],[181.92,182.16],[182.16,182.87],[182.87,183.11],[183.11,183.26],[183.26,184.21],[184.21,184.37],[184.37,184.84],[184.84,185.08],[185.08,185.32],[185.32,185.79],[185.79,185.87],[185.87,186.26],[186.26,186.5],[186.5,187.61]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Police violence across groups","start":189.03,"end":191.27,"words":[[189.08,189.51],[189.51,190.2],[190.2,190.63],[190.63,191.06]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Some analyses of police killings, adjusted for population, put Native Americans at or near the top of any group, followed by Black Americans; others rank them differently.","start":191.97,"end":203.87,"words":[[192.02,192.25],[192.25,192.95],[192.95,193.11],[193.11,193.49],[193.49,194.04],[194.31,194.93],[194.93,195.08],[195.08,196.01],[196.29,196.52],[196.52,196.98],[196.98,197.68],[197.68,197.84],[197.84,197.91],[197.91,198.15],[198.15,198.3],[198.3,198.54],[198.54,198.69],[198.69,198.92],[198.92,199.31],[199.58,200.05],[200.05,200.28],[200.28,200.59],[200.59,201.37],[201.64,201.95],[201.95,202.26],[202.26,202.49],[202.49,203.27]]},{"el":"s3","text":"The numbers are uncertain because race is often misrecorded for Native and Latino victims.","start":204.22,"end":210.63,"words":[[204.26,204.43],[204.43,204.95],[204.95,205.03],[205.03,205.63],[205.63,206.06],[206.06,206.4],[206.4,206.57],[206.57,206.92],[206.92,207.77],[207.77,207.94],[207.94,208.46],[208.46,208.71],[208.71,209.31],[209.31,210.0]]},{"el":"s3","text":"The map's police-killings layer (Mapping Police Violence) colors each case by the victim's race so you can see the pattern yourself.","start":210.98,"end":219.97,"words":[[211.02,211.2],[211.2,211.55],[211.55,212.52],[212.52,212.87],[212.87,213.31],[213.31,213.76],[213.76,214.46],[214.77,215.21],[215.21,215.48],[215.48,215.83],[215.83,216.09],[216.09,216.27],[216.27,216.89],[216.89,217.24],[217.24,217.51],[217.51,217.68],[217.68,217.95],[217.95,218.12],[218.12,218.3],[218.3,218.74],[218.74,219.36]]},{"el":"h4","text":"Standing together","start":220.87,"end":222.15,"words":[[220.92,221.47],[221.47,221.94]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Frederick Douglass spoke against Chinese exclusion in his 1869 “Composite Nation” speech.","start":222.85,"end":229.27,"words":[[222.85,223.44],[223.44,223.88],[223.88,224.25],[224.25,224.69],[224.69,225.2],[225.2,225.87],[225.87,226.01],[226.01,226.23],[226.23,227.33],[227.33,227.92],[227.92,228.36],[228.36,228.8]]},{"el":"s4","text":"In 1965, Filipino farmworkers led by Larry Itliong began the Delano grape strike and asked Cesar Chavez's Mexican American union to join; together they won the first major farmworker contracts.","start":229.62,"end":244.68,"words":[[229.67,229.84],[229.84,231.31],[231.6,232.34],[232.34,233.0],[233.0,233.24],[233.24,233.49],[233.49,233.82],[233.82,234.39],[234.39,234.8],[234.8,234.96],[234.96,235.54],[235.54,235.95],[235.95,236.44],[236.44,236.69],[236.69,237.01],[237.01,237.42],[237.42,238.08],[238.08,238.74],[238.74,239.39],[239.39,239.89],[239.89,240.05],[240.05,240.54],[240.83,241.32],[241.32,241.57],[241.57,241.81],[241.81,241.98],[241.98,242.3],[242.3,242.8],[242.8,243.37],[243.37,244.19]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Japanese American activist Yuri Kochiyama worked alongside Malcolm X and was with him when he was killed.","start":245.03,"end":252.2,"words":[[245.07,245.7],[245.7,246.33],[246.33,246.95],[246.95,247.27],[247.27,247.97],[247.97,248.29],[248.29,248.91],[248.91,249.38],[249.38,249.62],[249.62,249.85],[249.85,250.09],[250.09,250.32],[250.32,250.56],[250.56,250.79],[250.79,250.95],[250.95,251.18],[251.18,251.58]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Black, Latino, Asian and Native organizers worked together in the 1960s and 1970s, and the CAREN Act protects all of them.","start":252.55,"end":262.52,"words":[[252.6,252.98],[253.24,253.85],[254.11,254.49],[254.49,254.72],[254.72,255.18],[255.18,255.86],[255.86,256.16],[256.16,256.62],[256.62,256.77],[256.77,256.92],[256.92,257.99],[257.99,258.21],[258.21,259.43],[259.69,259.92],[259.92,260.07],[260.07,260.45],[260.45,260.68],[260.68,261.29],[261.29,261.44],[261.44,261.59],[261.59,261.89]]}]}